    "model": "Activity: tennis. 1. Before the match, ten minutes of imagery of serving and rallying well. Rationale: rehearsing success builds confidence and reduces cognitive anxiety. 2. During the match, a routine between points: turn away, two deep breaths, a cue word ('next') and a look at the strings. Rationale: it controls arousal and refocuses concentration after errors, so one bad point does not lead to another. 3. After the match, a written review of three things that went well and one to improve, with a confidence rating out of ten. Rationale: reflection keeps motivation and confidence up and the ratings show whether the plan is working.",
