    "marks": 6,
    "model": "A short-term goal is achieved within a few days or weeks and is broken into steps. A performance goal is a personal standard of performance that is independent of other performers. Activity: basketball. Short-term performance goal: by the next competition, raise free-throw success in training from the baseline recorded in the first analysis to 75% (illustrative figure), measured out of a set number of attempts in each session. The goal is specific to the free throw, measurable through the success rate, achievable with the planned drills, realistic for the training time available, and time-bound by the competition date.",
